The Template Method design pattern is implemented by defining a common algorithm structure in an abstract class, with specific steps left to be implemented by subclasses. Below is the complete implementation of the pattern for sorting algorithms.

---

### ✅ **Abstract Class: `SortAlgorithm`**

```java
public abstract class SortAlgorithm {
    // Abstract method to compare two elements
    public abstract int compare(Object a, Object b);

    // Abstract method to swap two elements in an array
    public abstract void swap(Object[] array, int i, int j);

    // Template method that defines the algorithm's skeleton
    public void sort(Object[] array) {
        for (int i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < array.length - 1 - i; j++) {
                if (compare(array[j], array[j + 1]) > 0) {
                    swap(array, j, j + 1);
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

